# Local IPOs: the IPO dialog and the chirps. Lists a candidate with the dialog and notices let
# through: the dialog opens, pauses the game and states the offering; closing it puts the pause
# back. The city buys 10 shares, the first trading day and a buy-out are chirped, and the buy-out
# pays the city for its shares. Costs the city nothing (the buy-out pays more than was spent);
# everything listed is removed in cleanup.
name local ipos: the IPO dialog opens and pauses; IPO, first day and buy-out are chirped
local-ipos on
ipo-healthy-days 1
ipo-scan
notices on
ipo-dialog on
ipo-list-now
expect-log notices: chirped [City Brokerage]
expect-log is going public at
wait 1
expect-visible FinanceOverhaulIpoDialog
# the look of the game's celebration dialogs: a banner with a large headline
expect-text FinanceOverhaulIpoDialogCongrats Congratulations!
expect-text FinanceOverhaulIpoDialogTitle is going public
# where it stands: its kind, then the street, cross street and district it has
expect-visible FinanceOverhaulIpoDialogWhere
expect-text FinanceOverhaulIpoDialogPrice a share
expect-text FinanceOverhaulIpoDialogCanBuy up to 1,000 shares (a 10% stake,
expect-text FinanceOverhaulIpoDialogWindow 7 days · until
expect-no-overflow FinanceOverhaulIpoDialog
expect-no-overflow FinanceOverhaulIpoDialogBanner
capture ipo-dialog
click FinanceOverhaulIpoDialogClose
expect-hidden FinanceOverhaulIpoDialog
ipo-buy 10
ipo-first-day
expect-log on its first trading day
ipo-buyout
expect-log The city received
expect-log for its 10 shares
expect-company gone unlisted
# bought out: the building is as it was before the company listed (no Historical tick left behind)
expect-headquarters as-before
cleanup:
ipo-dialog close
ipo-remove-test
notices off
local-ipos restore
